+**TargetProofBinding (strict at every object boundary):** stable IDs use
+`^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_-]{2,127}$`; prefixed hashes use `^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$`.
+
+| Fields | Shape / population |
+|---|---|
+| `binding_version` | required integer constant `1` |
+| `outcome_id`, `caller_id`, `path_id`, `authority_ref` | required stable IDs |
+| `caller_kind` | required: `product`, `operator`, `system`, `harness` |
+| `entrypoint` | required non-empty string |
+| `authority_role` | required: `authoritative`, `projection`, `legacy`, `emergency`, `retiring`, `dead` |
+| `caller_equivalence_ref` | non-empty string or null; defaults null |
+| `producer_contract`, `consumer_contract` | strict contract references or null; default null |
+| `runtime_chain_required` | boolean or null; defaults null |
+| `runtime_slots`, `predecessor_path_ids` | unique stable-ID arrays; default `[]` |
+| `terminal_oracle` | strict terminal oracle or null; defaults null |
+| `negative_oracle_ref` | non-empty string or null; defaults null |
+| `equivalence_group` | stable ID or null; defaults null |
+| `fixture_provenance` | array of strict provenance objects; defaults `[]` |
+
+A contract reference requires non-empty strings `owner`, `name`, `version`, `source_ref`,
+and a prefixed `sha256`. A terminal oracle requires a non-empty, unique `accepted_states`
+array of non-empty strings and a non-empty `reconciliation_authority` string. Each fixture
+provenance object requires non-empty strings `boundary`, `source`, `claim_ceiling`, and
+`kind` from `none`, `real-source`, `recorded`, `constructed`, `stub`, `mock`.
+
+At `nl` and `acceptance`, only the identity core (the first five rows above) is required.
+At `concrete`, a present binding must supply every field; `producer_contract`,
+`consumer_contract`, `runtime_chain_required`, `terminal_oracle`, `negative_oracle_ref`,
+and `equivalence_group` must be non-null. Missing fields are schema errors naming the
+field. `caller_equivalence_ref` may remain null for any caller kind: equivalence proof
+is checked by compiler/promotion consumers, not inferred by this shape. List fields may
+be empty except `runtime_slots` must be non-empty at `concrete` when
+`runtime_chain_required=true`. A legacy record with no binding remains valid at any maturity
+and visibly dumps `target_binding:null`, `target_binding_status:"legacy-unbound"`.
+
+**CodeRunEvidence.target_observation:** optional, defaults null. A present observation is
+strict, runner-owned, and requires all of these fields:
+
+| Fields | Type |
+|---|---|
+| `runtime_receipt_id`, `pid_start_time` | string |
+| `pid` | integer; no string or boolean coercion |
+| `outcome_id`, `caller_id`, `path_id`, `authority_ref_observed` | stable ID |
+| `entrypoint_observed`, `terminal_state` | string |
+| `producer_contract_hash`, `consumer_contract_hash` | prefixed SHA-256 hash |
+
+Only code receipts carry this object; other evidence tiers retain their existing shapes.
+Observation capture and comparison to expectations belong to the runner and downstream
+validation. The schema describes the payload and rejects unknown owner-added keys.
